o [andybunn] kalman.ar() and kalman.spec(): evolutive AR spectra by the
  Kalman filter, asked for by Ed Cook. First version written 2026-10-07 from
  Kitagawa and Gersch (1985), not from Ed's programs. Ed's reply: his
  are two programs (coefficients, then spectrum); he picks the order by
  trying several, not by AIC, and used AR(30) for sunspots. He offered
  to show them at the LTRR in November. Still open:
  - Compare with Ed's programs when we see them: how he sets the state
    noise, how he starts the filter, whether he smooths or only filters.
  - Compare with TSSS::tvar() and tvspc() (not installed here).
  - Maximum likelihood gives lambda = 0 for sunspot.year at order 30;
    the picture Ed describes needs lambda set by hand (about 1e-3).
    Decide what guidance to give on choosing it. profile() on a fit
    (added 2026-10-07) shows the likelihood over lambda.
  - variance = "varying" added 2026-10-07 (innovation variance as a
    random walk in log, from the prediction errors). It is a two-step
    estimate, smooth, and understates sharp changes. It does not
    respond to slow swings such as ca533 near 1400: those are not a
    change in one-step predictability. A wavelet shows them; this
    model does not, whatever the options.
  - A test against surrogates from the fixed-coefficient model, so a
    hand-set lambda can be judged. In trials the hand-set pictures for
    sunspot.year and ca533 were no more variable than surrogates.
  - One internal NA costs order + 1 years. Carrying y in the state
    would avoid that.
  - No significance test and no confidence band on the surface.
  - The plot does not mark where the coefficients are poorly
    determined (the ends); se is in the object.
  - Filter is in R: about 1 s for 2000 years at order 30 ("rw1"),
    3 s for "rw2". Move to C only if that becomes a problem.

